<article class="env-lemma" id="06ZP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06ZP">Lemma <span data-tag="06ZP">46.6.3</span>.</a> Let $f : T \to S$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of schemes. For any parasitic adequate $\mathcal{O}_ T$-module on $(\mathit{Sch}/T)_\tau $ the pushforward $f_*\mathcal{F}$ and the higher direct images $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ are parasitic adequate $\mathcal{O}_ S$-modules on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have already seen in Lemma <a href="/tag/06VR" data-tag="06VR">46.5.12</a> that these higher direct images are adequate. Hence it suffices to show that $(R^ if_*\mathcal{F})(U_ i) = 0$ for any $\tau $-covering $\{ U_ i \to S\} $ open. And $R^ if_*\mathcal{F}$ is parasitic by Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/07AG" data-tag="07AG">35.12.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>